+{"id":"audit.kit-row-reorder-undo","title":"Legacy Kit row reorder clears undo history","description":"Verified side effect, not established as a bug: both the two-audition-pad Vertical press branch and Audition + Mute + Vertical turn drag call deleteAllLogs before reordering. Review whether these legacy paths should match the newer undoable row workflow; do not infer all reorder gestures share its undo contract.","bindingIds":["instrument.reorder-press","instrument.drag-row-turn"],"sources":[{"file":"src/deluge/gui/views/instrument_clip_view.cpp","symbol":"InstrumentClipView::buttonAction"},{"file":"src/deluge/gui/views/instrument_clip_view.cpp","symbol":"InstrumentClipView::scrollVertical_dragSelectedNoteRow","anchor":"actionLogger.deleteAllLogs()"}],"status":"needs-review","device":"not-tested"}
+{"id":"audit.clip-transpose-undo","title":"Whole-Clip transposition clears undo after a successful move","description":"Verified behavior difference: commandTransposeKey clears undo history after nudgeNotesVertically succeeds, while a rejected out-of-range move leaves history alone. This is an explicit source policy, not proof of accidental corruption. Review consistency with note-edit moves and any newer undo support.","bindingIds":["instrument.transpose-octave","instrument.transpose-step","automation.clip-transpose"],"sources":[{"file":"src/deluge/gui/views/instrument_clip_view.cpp","symbol":"InstrumentClipView::commandTransposeKey","anchor":"actionLogger.deleteAllLogs()"}],"status":"needs-review","device":"not-tested"}
+{"id":"audit.note-code-rejected-undo","title":"Auditioned note-code editing clears undo before validation","description":"Potential avoidable undo loss: offsetNoteCodeAction clears all logs before checking whether a scale degree may move. A rejected degree move or melodic non-scale request can therefore erase undo without changing the requested pitch. Kit Drum reassignment also uses this helper. Device confirmation and intended undo policy remain unresolved.","bindingIds":["instrument.note-code"],"sources":[{"file":"src/deluge/gui/views/instrument_clip_view.cpp","symbol":"InstrumentClipView::offsetNoteCodeAction","anchor":"actionLogger.deleteAllLogs()"}],"status":"needs-review","device":"not-tested"}
+{"id":"audit.automation-clipboard-edges","title":"Automation Horizontal clipboard handling runs on both edges","description":"Potential duplicate action: while Learn remains held, handleHorizontalEncoderButtonAction copies or pastes without testing its on argument. A full Horizontal press and release can invoke the operation twice. Releasing Shift between edges can change paste into copy on release. Earlier dispatch and modifier-release order determine actual reachability; no device reproduction yet.","bindingIds":["automation.horizontal-copy.down","automation.horizontal-copy.up","automation.horizontal-paste.down","automation.horizontal-paste.up"],"sources":[{"file":"src/deluge/gui/views/automation_view.cpp","symbol":"AutomationView::handleHorizontalEncoderButtonAction","anchor":"Buttons::isButtonPressed(deluge::hid::button::LEARN)"}],"status":"needs-review","device":"not-tested"}
+{"id":"audit.dx7-fallback-feature-guard","title":"DX7 creation guard differs in the fallback handler","description":"Potential feature-gate inconsistency: InstrumentClipView::handleInstrumentChange tests EnableDX7Engine for Mod 7 + Synth, while InstrumentClipMinder::buttonAction's fallback DX7 branch does not. This establishes a handler difference, not universal bypass: verify which screens forward this gesture to the fallback when the feature is disabled.","bindingIds":["instrument.new-dx7","instrument-minder.output.new-dx7"],"sources":[{"file":"src/deluge/gui/views/instrument_clip_view.cpp","symbol":"InstrumentClipView::handleInstrumentChange","anchor":"EnableDX7Engine"},{"file":"src/deluge/model/clip/instrument_clip_minder.cpp","symbol":"InstrumentClipMinder::buttonAction"}],"status":"needs-review","device":"not-tested"}
+{"id":"audit.keyboard-sidebar-release-hold","title":"Keyboard release may erase the sidebar long-hold distinction","description":"Potential release-order bug, carried from the source-reviewed canonical verification.findings: KeyboardScreen::padAction clears padPressHeld before evaluateActiveNotes on release. Velocity, Mod and Scale restoration and Chord hold restoration consult that flag downstream, so their long-hold restoration branches appear unreachable through this path. Hardware reproduction and other callers remain to be checked.","bindingIds":["keyboard.sidebar.velocity.release","keyboard.sidebar.mod.release","keyboard.sidebar.scale.release","keyboard.sidebar.chord.restore"],"sources":[{"file":"src/deluge/gui/ui/keyboard/keyboard_screen.cpp","symbol":"KeyboardScreen::padAction","anchor":"pressedPads[idx].padPressHeld = false;"},{"file":"src/deluge/gui/ui/keyboard/column_controls/velocity.cpp","symbol":"VelocityColumn::handlePad","anchor":"pad.padPressHeld"},{"file":"src/deluge/gui/ui/keyboard/column_controls/mod.cpp","symbol":"ModColumn::handlePad","anchor":"pad.padPressHeld"},{"file":"src/deluge/gui/ui/keyboard/column_controls/scale_mode.cpp","symbol":"ScaleModeColumn::handlePad","anchor":"pad.padPressHeld"},{"file":"src/deluge/gui/ui/keyboard/column_controls/chord.cpp","symbol":"ChordColumn::handlePad","anchor":"pad.padPressHeld"}],"status":"needs-review","device":"not-tested"}
+{"id":"audit.menu-select-edge","title":"Context menus activate on Select down; SoundEditor activates on up","description":"Verified UI difference, not itself a bug: ContextMenu::buttonAction accepts on Select press in its allowed modes. SoundEditor::buttonAction normally activates on release only when selectButtonPressUsedUp is false. Review cross-screen press ownership and documentation before unifying these rules; the source difference alone does not prove double activation.","bindingIds":["menu.context.accept","menu.sound.select"],"sources":[{"file":"src/deluge/gui/context_menu/context_menu.cpp","symbol":"ContextMenu::buttonAction","anchor":"if (on && isUIModeWithinRange"},{"file":"src/deluge/gui/ui/sound_editor.cpp","symbol":"SoundEditor::buttonAction","anchor":"if (!on && !Buttons::selectButtonPressUsedUp)"}],"status":"needs-review","device":"not-tested"}
+{"id":"audit.midi-learn-cc-threshold","title":"CC learning accepts different value thresholds","description":"Verified target-specific difference: global MIDI Command learning accepts any nonzero CC value; External Step/Reset learning requires value >= 64. A controller sending only values 1–63 can learn a global command but not Step/Reset. This may intentionally distinguish a switch's active half-range; review expected controller compatibility rather than treating it as a confirmed bug.","bindingIds":["menu.midi.command.learn-cc","menu.midi.external-step.learn-cc"],"sources":[{"file":"src/deluge/gui/menu_item/midi/command.cpp","symbol":"Command::learnCC","anchor":"if (value != 0)"},{"file":"src/deluge/gui/menu_item/midi/external_step.cpp","symbol":"Input::learnCC","anchor":"if (value >= 64)"}],"status":"needs-review","device":"not-tested"}
